      "text": "### Kohn-Sham Equations"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-COMPUTATIONAL-MATERIALS.md#010",
      "path": [
        "09-COMPUTATIONAL-MATERIALS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:materials:09-computational-materials, git-history:materials:09-computational-materials]",
        "canonical_path": "materials/09-COMPUTATIONAL-MATERIALS.md",
        "concepts": "[computational, materials]",
        "current_path": "materials/09-COMPUTATIONAL-MATERIALS.md",
        "id": "maxim:materials:computational-materials",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "materials",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[computational, materials]",
        "section": "materials",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Computational Materials Science",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Kohn-Sham (1965): replace interacting electrons with               │\n│  non-interacting electrons in an effective potential                │\n│                                                                     │\n│  [-ℏ²/2m ∇² + V_eff(r)] φᵢ(r) = εᵢ φᵢ(r)                            │\n│                                                                     │\n│  V_eff = V_ext + V_Hartree + V_xc                                   │\n│    V_ext:     external (nuclear) potential                          │\n│    V_Hartree: electron-electron Coulomb (mean field)                │\n│    V_xc:      exchange-correlation correction                       │\n│                                                                     │\n│  ρ(r) = Σᵢ |φᵢ(r)|²   (sum over occupied orbitals)                  │\n│                                                                     │\n│  SELF-CONSISTENT FIELD (SCF) LOOP:                                  │\n│    Guess ρ → compute V_eff → solve KS equations → new ρ → repeat    │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\nSCF convergence is a fixed-point iteration (rho -> F(rho) -> fixed point). Anderson mixing (also called DIIS — direct inversion in the iterative subspace) accelerates convergence by using the history of residuals to extrapolate toward the fixed point, analogous to Krylov subspace methods in linear algebra. Convergence is not guaranteed in general but is reliable for most materials with appropriate mixing parameters.\n```"
    },
